S642 Goldbach/Lemoine same-pair projection
==========================================

Definitions
-----------
For odd primes p,q:
  even projection E = p + q
  odd projection  O = p + 2q, where q is the doubled coordinate
The two projections invert the ordered pair:
  q = O - E
  p = 2E - O
So an even E and odd O share a pair exactly when O-E and 2E-O
are odd primes.  Necessarily E < O < 2E.

Swapping the pair fixes E and reflects odd shadows:
  (p,q) <-> (q,p) sends O <-> 3E - O.
The duplicate diagonal p=q is the fixed locus O = 3E/2.

Duplicate diagonal p -> (2p,3p)
--------------------------------
  p=3   even=2p=6   odd=3p=9  
  p=5   even=2p=10  odd=3p=15 
  p=7   even=2p=14  odd=3p=21   <== p=7 gives the 14/21 shadow
  p=11  even=2p=22  odd=3p=33 
  p=13  even=2p=26  odd=3p=39 
  p=17  even=2p=34  odd=3p=51 
